      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg per day, which is double the usual adult maximum of 3,200 mg per day. At that dose, the risks include GI bleeding, kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention. The patient's normal kidney and liver function lowers some of that risk, but it doesn't make this dose appropriate.\n\nAlso, medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber, so this needs to go through the medicine team.\n\nHere are some options for the prescriber to consider:\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the usual maximum), or\n- **400\u2013800 mg by mouth every 6\u20138 hours** as needed for pain, with the daily maximum stated.\n\nIf the prescriber confirms 1600 mg four times daily is intended, they can enter it directly or ask me to enter it with a note documenting their rationale. I'd still recommend they verify the dose first."
      }
     ],
